        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): dripping model pulls hang past idle timeout during setup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where OpenClaw Ollama setup could hang forever while downloading a model when `/api/pull` kept sending occasional NDJSON progress lines that never advanced `completed`.\n\nAffected workflow: Ollama provider setup / `ensureOllamaModelPulled` model download.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOllama setup already aborts if headers never arrive (30s) and already fails if the pull stream goes fully idle (300s). After headers return, that response timer was cleared, so only the per-chunk idle timer remained. Idle resets on every chunk, so a slow drip can keep the download alive indefinitely.\n\nThis keeps the headers and byte-idle budgets as-is, then arms a **no-progress watchdog** after the first body chunk. The watchdog resets only when aggregate Ollama `completed` increases. Status-only post-download finalization gets **one non-renewable grace arm**; further status-only lines (including distinct novel freeform statuses) cannot renew it, so:\n- non-advancing drips fail closed\n- advancing large/slow downloads may continue past any fixed wall-clock lifetime\n- healthy finite finalization phases survive inside one grace window\n- cycling or novel status drips without completed progress cannot act as an unlimited keepalive\n\nOptional `streamNoProgressTimeoutMs` / `streamIdleTimeoutMs` on `ensureOllamaModelPulled` are for tests only.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDuring Ollama setup, a wedged or maliciously dripping /api/pull stream fails closed with a no-progress error. Healthy pulls that keep advancing completed survive. Finite status-only finalization survives within one grace budget. Distinct novel status drips without completed progress are bounded — removing the prior availability hang bypass.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `6b2f322c48e`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Ollama setup `/api/pull` no longer hangs when status-only NDJSON drips without advancing `completed` (including distinct novel status strings).\n- Real environment tested: local Node function tests via Vitest fake timers against `ensureOllamaModelPulled` (mocked fetch streams).\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n\n```bash\nnode ./node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-providers.config.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.pull.test.ts\n```\n\n- Evidence after fix:\n\n```text\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n   Duration  20.93s\n```\n\n- Observed result after fix: non-advancing drip, cycling status, and distinct novel status drips all abort with the no-progress message; advancing completed and finite status-only finalization within one grace still succeed.\n- What was not tested: live local Ollama daemon pull; loopback HTTP suite not re-run in this round (function-level fake-timer coverage only).\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Cursor).",
